    "body": "Branch refreshed against current main (kernel #3630 landed) and gate green:\n\n- \\camcraft-motion\\ lib: 624 passed; \\\rotary_flow\\: 8 passed\n- \\camcraft-app\\ lib: 307 passed; \\operations\\: 125 passed; \\project_roundtrip\\: 83 passed (the v80 round trip)\n- \\\ribbon\\: 13 passed; \\\rotary_flow_band\\: 4 passed; \\\rotary_stated_axis\\: 9 passed; \\\rotary_letter\\: 3 passed; \\\rotary_verify\\: 10 passed; \\\rotary_parallel_keyway\\: 1 passed; \\setup_align_multiaxis\\: 11 passed; \\continuous_4axis_part\\: 10 passed (regenerated for v80)\n- \\camcraft-ui\\ lib: 1588 passed\n- clippy on motion, app, ui, sim, \\--all-targets\\, \\-D warnings\\: clean\n\nThe PR opens when parent #3674 merges, per the stacking rule.\n\nReconciliation against main's final kernel form:\n- main's kind registry appended the waterjet profile (46) and the multi-axis deburr (47); Rotary Flow now seats at ordinal 48, digest tag 48.\n- main's project file took v78 for the stored tool reservations (#2604); the stated rotation axis moves to v79 and the Rotary Flow arm to v80 (\\PROJECT_VERSION = 80\\).\n- main's kernel review added the swept-ball guard (\\\rotary_flow_guard\\); the band test fixture now revolves the bar over 72 facets, the kernel tests' own count.\n- main's new cut-recipe law (\\\recipe.rs\\) takes the Rotary Flow arm: no params coordinates, the picks ride the op's own selection.\n\nThe \\cargo xtask gate quick\\ per-crate prebuild wedged (#3675): one corrupt \\\boa_engine\\ artifact, then two out-of-memory link failures (os error 1455). The suites above ran per binary instead, and clippy ran separately. Record this for the PR body later. Worktree \\\target/\\ cleaned.",
